# Issue: independent defs were ordered by AId (string-intern order) in the def
# sorts of AExpand, ASyntaxUtil and the Verilog, lambda-calculus and SAL
# foreign-call blocks, and in the def list AConv built from its maps.
# Fix: SCC.tsortStable breaks ties by input position and AConv emits its defs
# in elaboration order, so the output order depends on the design alone.
# Pull request: https://github.com/MatX-inc/bsc/pull/195
# Probe: each module's Verilog alone versus behind two scramblers; unfixed,
# ForeignOrder's inlined defs and SelectOrder's select blocks come out swapped.

batching_verilog_pair ForeignOrder.bsv mkForeignOrder ForeignOrderTop.bsv mkForeignOrderTop {ForeignOrderScrambleA.bsv ForeignOrderScrambleB.bsv}

# SelectOrder's two select always blocks tie in the def sort; batch order
# B, A broke the old tie by AId, and A, B the def list order AConv took
# from its maps, so the probe is run behind both tops.
batching_verilog_pair SelectOrder.bsv mkSelectOrder SelectOrderTopBA.bsv mkSelectOrderTopBA {SelectOrderScrambleA.bsv SelectOrderScrambleB.bsv}

erase SelectOrder.bo
erase SelectOrderScrambleA.bo
erase SelectOrderScrambleB.bo
erase mkSelectOrder.v
compile_verilog_pass SelectOrderTopAB.bsv mkSelectOrderTopAB
compare_file mkSelectOrder.v mkSelectOrder.oneshot.v
